# Candidate binary coordinates for the SU₃(5) coset module

The packed rows were extracted from the retained literal upper-Borel GAP
calculation. `source/generate.py` records the deterministic change of basis:
the constant vector, 104 further vectors of the retained subspace, 20 further
augmentation vectors, and one vector of augmentation one. These definitions
alone assert neither a group realization nor any matrix identity or simplicity.

Matrices act on columns. `permutationImages` lists GAP right-coset images;
on inverse left cosets the function action sends v(i) to v(p(i)). Thus the
full matrices are C⁻¹ P C, where columns of C are the adapted basis.
The middle diagonal blocks have indices [1,105) and [105,125).

Source motivation: Guralnick–Malle, Classification of 2F-modules I,
Proposition 4.3; Aschbacher–Smith K.2, printed p.453.
-/

